      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: stupid_americans_meme; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The image features a person in a Marvin the Martian costume holding a rocket, with overlaid text reading 'stupid americans.. they elect their enemy to rule over them.' The meme uses a popular cartoon character to mock American political processes, implying that voters are choosing their adversaries. This is a hateful message that targets American citizens as a group, using derogatory language and a dismissive tone to express disdain for the political system and its electorate. The intent is to provoke anger or reinforce negative stereotypes about American voters and their choices, fitting the definition of a hateful meme as it attacks a group based on nationality and political behavior.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_87dbfdf9"
